{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2186-06-02 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. Smith. I'm Dr. Lee, one of your hospitalists. You're here today for your high-dose methotrexate treatment for CNS lymphoma. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2186-06-02 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Morning, Doctor. I’m doing okay. Just the usual tinnitus, but nothing new or concerning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2186-06-02 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Glad to hear you're feeling stable. We’ll be giving you methotrexate today after some IV fluids to protect your kidneys. You’ve been on this before, so you know the routine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2186-06-02 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve done this many times. I brought my Temodar with me—I started it at home yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2186-06-02 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’ll make sure it’s documented. We’re also planning to place a Port-a-cath later this week to make future infusions easier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2186-06-02 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, right. I forgot that was scheduled. Is it necessary? I mean, my veins have held up so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2186-06-02 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s safer and more comfortable long-term. With repeated chemo, veins can get damaged. This will give us reliable access and reduce discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2186-06-02 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. When will it be done?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2186-06-02 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Scheduled for Thursday morning. You’ll be under light sedation, and it usually takes about 20 minutes. No major risks, but we’ll monitor you after."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2186-06-02 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, I trust the team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2186-06-02 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve started your IV fluids with sodium bicarbonate to alkalinize your urine. This helps clear the methotrexate safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2186-06-02 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Same as last time. Any changes in dose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2186-06-02 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Still 8 grams per square meter. Your body size puts it at about 19,360 mg. We’ll start the infusion in an hour."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2186-06-02 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a big number. But I know it’s targeted."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2186-06-02 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And we’ll start leucovorin rescue 24 hours after to protect your healthy cells."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2186-06-02 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting the methotrexate infusion now. It’ll run over several hours. Let us know if you feel any nausea, chills, or discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2186-06-02 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I’ll let you know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2186-06-03 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs show your sodium is starting to drop—from 137 yesterday to 134 this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2186-06-03 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that a problem? I feel fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2186-06-03 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s something we watch closely. Because you have diabetes insipidus and are on desmopressin, the large IV fluids can cause your body to retain too much water."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2186-06-03 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the desmopressin is making it worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2186-06-03 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Temporarily, yes. We may need to hold a dose to let your body correct the balance. We’ll check again in a few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2186-06-03 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your sodium dropped further—to 127. We’re going to hold your evening desmopressin dose and stop the IV fluids now that the methotrexate is cleared."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2186-06-03 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I still feel okay. But I trust you’re doing the right thing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2186-06-03 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We are. We’ll give you a small dose of salt through the IV to help bring it up safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2186-06-04 06:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your sodium is improving. It’s up to 130 now. We’ll keep monitoring, but you’re on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2186-06-04 06:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2186-06-04 06:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely tomorrow. We’ll check one more methotrexate level today. Once it’s low enough, and your sodium stays stable, you’re good to go."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2186-06-04 06:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the Port-a-cath?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2186-06-04 06:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Still scheduled for tomorrow morning. You’ll go right after, once you’re awake and stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2186-06-04 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your last methotrexate level is 0.08—that’s excellent. It means the drug is cleared and you’re safe to stop leucovorin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2186-06-04 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. So I’m ready for the Port-a-cath and then home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2186-06-04 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. The procedure team will see you tonight to go over consent, and you’ll have it first thing in the morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2186-06-05 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You had the Port-a-cath placed successfully an hour ago. The catheter is in the right atrium, and it’s working well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2186-06-05 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t even feel it. How’s the site?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2186-06-05 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Looks clean and dry. You’ll need to keep it dry for a few days, and we’ll check it at your next visit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2186-06-05 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Any restrictions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2186-06-05 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Avoid heavy lifting on that side for a week. Otherwise, you can resume normal activity."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2186-06-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re finalizing your discharge. Your sodium is stable at 130, and you’re back on your regular desmopressin dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2186-06-05 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the low sodium was just from the fluids and desmopressin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2186-06-05 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. It’s a common issue in patients like you. We managed it by holding fluids and a dose of desmopressin. It should stay normal now at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2186-06-05 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. What about the Temodar?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2186-06-05 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue as prescribed—240 mg daily for seven days, then seven off. We’ve added ondansetron in case you feel nauseous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2186-06-05 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had it before. Usually not too bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2186-06-05 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, take the sodium bicarbonate tablets the day before your next methotrexate—two every four to six hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2186-06-05 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Same as before. I have it written down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2186-06-05 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll follow up with oncology in two weeks for your next methotrexate and rituximab."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2186-06-05 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my eye check-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2186-06-05 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You said your ophthalmologist cleared you recently—no signs of intraocular lymphoma. Keep that follow-up as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2186-06-05 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, all good there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2186-06-05 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. We’ll send all instructions and meds with you. Call if you have confusion, seizures, or severe nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2186-06-05 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2186-06-05 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great. Take care, and we’ll see you in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2186-06-05 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before discharge—how are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2186-06-05 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really well. No headaches, no dizziness. Ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2186-06-05 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Your neuro exam is stable, blood pressure is good, and you’re walking independently."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2186-06-05 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been doing my walks every day here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2186-06-05 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That helps a lot. Keep it up. And remember—resume all your usual meds, including desmopressin, as before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2186-06-05 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2186-06-05 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Safe travels home. We’ll see you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2186-06-05 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your labs from this morning show your liver enzymes were a bit high but are improving. Likely from the chemo, not a concern now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2186-06-05 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had that before. They bounce back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2186-06-05 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll watch them, but no action needed now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2186-06-05 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2186-06-05 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And your calcium and magnesium were low but corrected with supplements. We’ll check them next time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2186-06-05 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll keep taking the calcium pills."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2186-06-05 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, please do. All set—discharge papers are ready."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2186-06-02 08:38:00",
    "admission_end": "2186-06-05 18:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 65-year-old man with a history of CNS lymphoma and diabetes insipidus was admitted for elective high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy as part of reinduction therapy following disease recurrence. He presented in stable condition with only chronic tinnitus and no acute symptoms. He received methotrexate 8 g/m² with standard urinary alkalinization and IV hydration. Leucovorin rescue was initiated 24 hours post-infusion, and methotrexate levels declined appropriately to 0.08 by discharge. His hospital course was complicated by asymptomatic hyponatremia, dropping to 123, attributed to desmopressin use in the setting of high IV fluid volume. Management included holding IV fluids, withholding desmopressin temporarily, and administering IV sodium chloride, leading to improvement in sodium to 130. A Port-a-cath was successfully placed on hospital day 3 for future venous access. He remained neurologically stable, seizure-free, and hemodynamically normal throughout. He was discharged home with instructions to resume all home medications, continue temozolomide, and take sodium bicarbonate prior to next methotrexate dose, with follow-up in two weeks.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Diabetes insipidus",
      "Other disorders of neurohypophysis",
      "Other malignant lymphomas, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, without mention of intractable epilepsy",
      "Other genetic carrier status",
      "Personal history of tuberculosis"
    ]
  }
}
